   - `movie-list.component.ts` — `MovieListComponent` (imports `MatButtonModule`, `MatDatepickerModule`, `MatFormFieldModule`, `MatInputModule`); `minDate` (today at local midnight); `dayButtons` computed once via IIFE in field initializer (`Today` + next 4 weekdays via `addDays`/`weekdayFull`); `selectedDate` signal driven by `route.queryParamMap` subscription via `resolveSelectedDate(params.get('date'))`, triggering `loadMovies()` on each change; `datepickerValue` computed (`null` if `selectedDate` matches a day button, else a `Date`); `loading`/`error`/`movies`/`screenings` signals; `movieCards` computed (filters movies with ≥1 screening that day, screenings sorted by `time.localeCompare`); `loadMovies()` using `forkJoin({ movies: ..., screenings: ... })`; `selectDay(date)` does `router.navigate([], { relativeTo: this.route, queryParams: { date } })`; `onDatepickerChange(date)` converts to ISO and calls `selectDay`; `openScreening(screeningId)` navigates to seats route.
   - `movie-list.component.html` — `day-picker` container with `day-button` loop (`data-date`, `data-selected`) plus a `mat-form-field` (`data-testid="date-picker"`) wrapping a `matDatepicker` input with `[min]="minDate"`; then `@if/@else if` chain for `movies-loading` / `movies-error` + `movies-retry-button` / `movies-empty` / `movie-list` with `movie-card` loop (`movie-title`, `movie-genre`, `movie-runtime` = `"<n> min"`, `movie-format`, `screening-button` loop labelled with `screening.time`).
   - `movie-list.component.scss` — basic flex layout.

   **New files created (pages/summary):**
   - `summary.component.ts` — `SummaryComponent`; `screeningId` from `route.snapshot.paramMap`; `screening`/`movie` signals populated via `api.getScreening(id).pipe(switchMap(screening => api.getMovie(screening.movieId).pipe(map(movie => ({screening, movie})))))`, redirecting to `/` on error; `items`/`total` computed via `buildSummaryItems`/price sum; `formatPrice` re-exported for template use; `remove(item)` calls `bookingService.removeSeats(item.ids)` then navigates to seats route if the booking becomes empty; `back()`/`confirm()` simple navigations.
   - `summary.component.html` — `summary-title`, `summary-list` with `summary-item` divs (`summary-item-title`, `summary-item-datetime` = `"<date> <time>"`, `summary-item-row`, `summary-item-seat`, `summary-item-price`, `summary-item-remove-button`), `summary-total` = `"Total: <formatPrice(total())>"`, `back-button`/`confirm-button`.
   - `summary.component.scss`.

   **New files created (pages/checkout):**
   - `checkout.component.ts` — `CheckoutComponent` (imports `MatButtonModule`, `MatCheckboxModule`, `MatFormFieldModule`, `MatInputModule`); `screeningId` from route snapshot; `initialForm` read once from `bookingService.booking()?.form ?? emptyForm()`; per-field signals `firstName/lastName/email/confirmEmail/phone/termsAccepted` seeded from `initialForm`; `touched` record signal (all false initially); `submitting` signal; `items`/`total` computed via `buildSummaryItems`; computed error signals:
     ```ts
     protected readonly firstNameError = computed(() => requiredMinLength(this.firstName(), 'First name', 2));
     protected readonly lastNameError = computed(() => requiredMinLength(this.lastName(), 'Last name', 2));
     protected readonly emailError = computed(() => {
       const value = this.email();
       if (!value) return 'Email is required';
       return EMAIL_RE.test(value) ? null : 'Enter a valid email address';
     });
     protected readonly confirmEmailError = computed(() => {
       const value = this.confirmEmail();
       if (!value) return 'Confirm email is required';
       return value === this.email() ? null : 'Email addresses do not match';
     });
     protected readonly phoneError = computed(() => {
       const value = this.phone();
       if (!value) return null;
       return /^\d{9}$/.test(value) ? null : 'Phone number must be exactly 9 digits';
     });
     protected readonly termsError = computed(() => (this.termsAccepted() ? null : 'You must accept the terms and conditions'));
     ```
     with `EMAIL_RE = /^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/` module-level constant; `formValid` computed (all errors null); constructor registers an `effect()` that calls `bookingService.updateForm({...all 6 current signal values})` on every change (runs immediately too, harmlessly re-persisting initial values); `inputValue(event)` helper casts `event.target` to `HTMLInputElement`; `touch(field)` sets `touched` map; `onTermsChange(event: MatCheckboxChange)` sets `termsAccepted` + touches it; `back()` navigates to summary; `pay()` — if `submitting()` return; if `!formValid()`, mark all fields touched + `toast.show('The form contains errors')` + return (no request sent); else builds `CreateReservationPayload` with `seats: this.items().flatMap(item => item.ids)` (summary order, not insertion order), submits via `api.createReservation`, on success `markPaid(email)` + navigate to `/confirmation`, on error shows `'Payment failed. Please try again.'` toast and resets `submitting`.
   - `checkout.component.html` — five `.field` divs each with a `mat-form-field` containing a `mat-label` (`data-testid="*-label"`, text ending in ` *` for the 5 required fields, no asterisk for phone) and a native `<input matInput>` (`data-testid="*-input"`, bound via `[value]`/`(input)="field.set(inputValue($event))"`/`(blur)="touch('field')"`), each followed by a conditional `@if (touched().field && fieldError(); as msg)` error div (`data-testid="*-error"`); a `mat-checkbox` (`data-testid="terms-checkbox"`) with `[checked]`/`(change)="onTermsChange($event)"` wrapping a `<span data-testid="terms-label">`; `checkout-back-button`/`pay-button` (text toggles `"Processing…"` vs `"Pay " + formatPrice(total())`, `[disabled]="submitting()"`).
   - `checkout.component.scss`.

   **New files created (pages/confirmation):**
   - `confirmation.component.ts` — `ConfirmationComponent`; `email` computed from `bookingService.booking()?.customerEmail ?? ''`; `continue()` clears booking + navigates to `/`.
   - `confirmation.component.html`:
     ```html
     <h1 data-testid="confirmation-heading">Payment successful</h1>
     <p data-testid="confirmation-message">Your tickets will be sent shortly to {{ email() }}</p>
     <button mat-flat-button type="button" data-testid="confirmation-continue-button" (click)="continue()">Continue</button>
     ```
   - `confirmation.component.scss`.

4. Errors and fixes:
   - **`pnpm nx build cinescope` aborted with `ERR_PNPM_ABORTED_REMOVE_MODULES_DIR_NO_TTY`** on first attempt — pnpm wanted to recreate `node_modules` but refused without a TTY. **Fix:** prefixed the command with `CI=true` (e.g. `CI=true pnpm nx build cinescope`), which allowed pnpm to proceed non-interactively. This must be used for all subsequent `pnpm nx build`/`lint`/`test` invocations in this sandbox.
   - **Build failure: `Could not resolve "@angular/animations/browser"`** when `app.config.ts` included `provideAnimationsAsync()` from `@angular/platform-browser/animations/async`. Investigated and confirmed `@angular/animations` package is genuinely absent from `node_modules/@angular/` (only `cdk`, `common`, `compiler`, `compiler-cli`, `core`, `forms`, `material`, `platform-browser`, `router` are installed). Tried switching to `provideNoopAnimations()` from `@angular/platform-browser/animations` instead — got the **same class of error** (`@angular/platform-browser/fesm2022/animations.mjs` statically imports `@angular/animations/browser` even for the noop path). **Final fix:** removed all animation-provider imports/calls from `app.config.ts` entirely — no `provideAnimations`/`provideNoopAnimations`/`provideAnimationsAsync` call at all. Build then succeeded (verified bundle output, exit code 0). **This is a hard constraint going forward: never import from `@angular/platform-browser/animations` or `/animations/async` in this codebase.**
   - **Lint failure: `@angular-eslint/no-output-native` on `seat-row.component.ts:12`** — the `output<string[]>()` was originally named `toggle`, which collides with the native DOM `toggle` event name. **Fix:** renamed the output property to `seatToggle` in `seat-row.component.ts` (both the `readonly seatToggle = output<string[]>();` declaration and the `this.seatToggle.emit(ids);` call), and updated the template binding in `seat-selection.component.html` from `(toggle)="onToggle($event)"` to `(seatToggle)="onToggle($event)"`. Re-ran `CI=true pnpm nx lint cinescope` → `✔ All files pass linting`.
   - **No user feedback was received correcting my approach** — these were all self-discovered build/lint errors that I fixed without needing user input, since the user's only instruction was the original task description and explicit "do not ask questions" directive.
   - **json-server port confusion during manual testing** — an early backgrounded `(pnpm api > /tmp/api.log 2>&1 &)` subshell left an orphaned json-server process bound only to IPv6 loopback (`::1:3000`); my own `node -e "fetch('http://localhost:3000/...')"` test calls failed with `ECONNREFUSED` against `127.0.0.1`/`localhost` resolution, while `http://[::1]:3000/movies` succeeded and returned real data. A subsequent explicit `pnpm api` launch via the Bash tool's `run_in_background: true` then failed with `EADDRINUSE: address already in use ::1:3000`, confirming the orphaned instance was still alive and functional. **I left this orphaned json-server process running** (it serves data correctly) rather than killing it, and did not yet reconcile whether the actual browser (Chrome, via the dev server) will reach it fine over `localhost:3000` (it likely will, since browsers do dual-stack Happy Eyeballs resolution, but this was not yet empirically confirmed before the summary cutoff).

